      "writtenOn": "2026-04-24T20:21:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m inclined to say we don\u0027t land these. Historically we have opted to remove rsqrt and other low precision instructions: https://skia-review.git.corp.google.com/c/skia/+/396723 and in raster pipeline it uses the precise rsqrt when it\u0027s SK_CPU_X64_LEVEL_SSE2\n\nI think there is something to be said about consistency across platforms, in particular for CPU rasterization. Since your plan for rsqrt is more for geometry processing in prep for GPU rendering, one could argue that that consistency is less necessary because the GPU is going to make GPU diffs more unpredictable anyways.  But I could also see surprise precision issues creeping into geometry calculations that are hard to debug if it depends on a specific lower-precision rsqrt on a user\u0027s device compared to the one we are trying to repro on.",
      "parentUuid": "7be27cd3_8df707e1",
      "revId": "8a41acf24770bbfce9baca585e173a8c3b900d0f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1291d870_b860c932",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 3948337
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-24T20:25:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes I could improve accuracy by adding more newton-raphson steps, but that is likely to regress performance more. I\u0027ll abandon this, and if it comes up in the future we can resuscitate this patch. \n\n(Since my local benching is on my M4, which is NEON, I tried removing the newton-raphson step, and benchmarking on the 8-bit precision. Even then it still regressed performance.)",
      "parentUuid": "818efe03_78fedccd",
      "revId": "8a41acf24770bbfce9baca585e173a8c3b900d0f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
